# draper's `delegate_all` is a class method whose body is `include
# Draper::AutomaticDelegation`; a decorator's body calls it, and Ruby runs
# the include on that decorator. The mixin sat in a method, which DEC-097
# rightly records nowhere lexically, so `--ancestors CommentDecorator` lacked
# it and every delegated call was "no such method". A class body's call of
# a class macro that includes, prepends or extends a constant, unconditionally,
# adds that edge to the calling class; a subclass that never calls it gains
# nothing, and neither does an include behind a condition.
ancestors CommentDecorator CommentDecorator,AutomaticDelegation,Decorator
ancestors PlainDecorator PlainDecorator,Decorator
card CommentDecorator#delegated status=resolved
card PlainDecorator#delegated status=no_such_method
ancestors Item Item,Tracked,Record
card Item#tracked? status=resolved
card Item.find_tracked status=resolved
